;/sup&gt; largest =3D=3D (n - k)&lt;sup&gt;th&lt;/sup&gt; smallest' highlig=
hts the relationship between the kth largest and (n-k)th smallest elements,=
 where 'n' is the array's size. A horizontal arrow connects the initial arr=
ay to a partially sorted array `[2 1 3 4 5 6]`. This arrow is labeled `quic=
kselect(n - k)`, indicating that the `quickselect` function is applied to f=
